  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## C3. Dynamic centering, version 2: triple difference with an explicit reference group\n\nAll social locations are stacked into one model with institution \u00d7 year and group \u00d7 year fixed effects, so each coefficient is the New York post-2017 change for that group *relative to the reference group*, in log points. Following L\u00f3pez et al.'s logic of naming and justifying the reference group (p. 191), set `REF` below and say why in the write-up. Changing it and rerunning shows how much the narrative depends on that choice."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "REF = \"white_women\"   # justify in the report; try others to show sensitivity\n\nlong = panel.melt(id_vars=[\"unitid\", \"fall_year\", \"ny\", \"high_pell_inst\"], value_vars=SL,\n                  var_name=\"group\", value_name=\"count\")\nlong[\"log_count\"] = np.log(long[\"count\"] + 1)\nlong[\"post\"] = (long[\"fall_year\"] >= 2017).astype(int)\nlong[\"cell\"] = long[\"unitid\"].astype(str) + \"_\" + long[\"group\"]\nlong[\"inst_year\"] = long[\"unitid\"].astype(str) + \"_\" + long[\"fall_year\"].astype(str)\nlong[\"group_year\"] = long[\"group\"] + \"_\" + long[\"fall_year\"].astype(str)\n\ndef triple_diff(ref, data=long):\n    d = data.copy()\n    terms = []\n    for g in SL:\n        if g != ref:\n            d[f\"ddd_{g}\"] = d[\"ny\"] * d[\"post\"] * (d[\"group\"] == g).astype(int)\n            terms.append(f\"ddd_{g}\")\n    m = smf.ols(f\"log_count ~ {' + '.join(terms)} + C(cell) + C(inst_year) + C(group_year)\", data=d\n               ).fit(cov_type=\"cluster\", cov_kwds={\"groups\": d[\"unitid\"]})\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\"coef\": m.params[terms], \"se\": m.bse[terms], \"p\": m.pvalues[terms]})\n    out.index = [label(t.replace(\"ddd_\", \"\")) for t in terms]\n    out[\"approx_pct_diff_vs_ref\"] = (np.exp(out[\"coef\"]) - 1) * 100\n    return out\n\nddd = triple_diff(REF)\nprint(\"Reference group:\", label(REF))\nddd.round(3)"
